title: POST /repos/:repo/query/profile
tags: [[HTTP endpoint]] [[Slow log]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Runs a query exactly as POST /query does and answers its slow-log entry — phases, time, reads — whatever it cost.

```
POST /repos/:repo/query/profile      (the body of POST /repos/:repo/query)
→ {"entry": <entry>}
```

Runs the query exactly as `/query` does and answers, instead of its results, the
entry the slow log would hold for it ([[What the slow log records]]) — its
phases, their time and reads, its context — whatever it cost. The replay itself
is not logged: a slow query replayed is as slow, and not news. It is what
`mf slow replay` sends ([[Diagnosing a slow operation]]).

An entry says where the time went ''then''; this answers whether it still goes
there — after a fix, on a warm cache, on another machine — without copying the
query into a tool that opens the store, which the daemon holds locked.

An entry whose query was not kept whole (longer than 64 KiB, or logged before
queries were kept whole) cannot be replayed, and `mf slow replay` says so.
